TheZat the end of the date stands forZero time.

TheTin the middle is aseparatorbetween date and time.

UTC stands forUniversal Time Coordinated.

To obtain local time in world, you need to add or subtract hours from UTC
depending on how many time zones you are away from Greenwich.

An Instant can be created in several different ways:

You can create an Instant using thenew Temporal.Instant()constructor.

Thenat the end meansBigInt.

Theparametermust be aBigInt.

You can create an Instant from anRFC 9557 string.

TheZat the end of the time, is theISO 8601standard for formattingUTC time.

It indicates that the offset from UTC time is 0 (Zero).

It is also known asZtime,Zerotime orZulutime.

TheTin the middle is theISO 8601standard forseparatingdate and time.

You can create an Instant object from the number ofmilliseconds since the Unix epoch.

You can create an Instant object from the number ofnanoseconds since the Unix epoch.

JavaScript Temporal.Instant does not have any method for creating an instant from current time.

You must use a Temporal.Now method instead.

TheTemporal.Now.instant()method returns an Instant object with the exact current time.

WithDate, you useDate.now()to get the current
timestamp.

TheDate.now()method returns the timestamp value inmilliseconds:

WithTemporal, you useTemporal.Now.instant():

The propertyepochMillisecondsreturns the timestamp value inmilliseconds:

The propertyepochNanosecondsreturns the timestamp value innanoseconds:

All temporal objectshave their owncompare() method:

Most (*) temporal objectshave their ownequals() method:

(*) Duration has not.

ATemporal.Instantdoes not include time zone information.

You must convert it to aTemporal.ZonedDateTimeto display local time.

ThetoZonedDateTimeISO()method converts a UTC moment
to a specific time zone:

UTC is a global clock.

Time zone is the local view of the same clock.

UTC is used as a reference time:

### Code Snippets

```
const instant = Temporal.Instant.from("2026-05-17T14:30:00Z");

---

London:    12:00 (UTC)
Oslo:      14:00 (UTC+2)
New York:  08:00 (UTC-4)
Tokyo:     21:00 (UTC+9)

---

const instant = new Temporal.Instant(1779028200000000000n);

---

const instant = Temporal.Instant.from("2026-05-17T14:30:00Z");

---

const instant = Temporal.Instant.fromEpochMilliseconds(1779028200000);

---

const instant = Temporal.Instant.fromEpochNanoseconds(1779028200000000000n);

---

const instant = Temporal.Now.instant();

---

let timestamp = Date.now();

---

const instant = Temporal.Now.instant();
let timestamp = instant.epochMilliseconds;

